rule-name-prefix DQC

/** V32 Release **/
/**

Overview: The SEC Division of Economic and Risk Analysis has identified that Business Development Companies (BDCs) have tagged the investment income - interest and investment income - dividend line items in the consolidated statements of operations with the elements InvestmentIncomeInterest and InvestmentIncomeDividend.  These elements are defined as income on nonoperating securities.  For a BDC investment income is operating income and the appropriate elements are InterestIncomeOperating and DividendIncomeOperating.

See: https://www.sec.gov/about/divisions-offices/division-economic-risk-analysis/260827-dqr-inappropriate-elements-used-tag-bdc-consolidated-statements-operations

Rule US.0256.10979 identifies BDC filings using the element InvestmentIncomeInterest.  The element InterestIncomeOperating should be used.

Rule US.0256.10980 identifies BDC filings using the element InvestmentIncomeDividend.  The element DividendIncomeOperating should be used.

Rule US.0256.10981 identifies BDC filings using the element InvestmentIncomeInterestAndDividend.  The element InterestAndDividendIncomeOperating should be used.

A filing is identified as a BDC filing using the constant $BDC_FLAG which identifies filings that include a Schedule of Investments as a financial statement.

**/

ASSERT US.0256.10979 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not $BDC_FLAG
	skip
else

$fact1 = {@concept = InvestmentIncomeInterest}

exists($fact1)

message
"The filer is a business development company and has reported a value of {$fact1} using the element InvestmentIncomeInterest.  This element is defined as interest income on nonoperating securities.  For a business development company interest earned on investments is operating income and should be tagged using the element InterestIncomeOperating. Please replace the element InvestmentIncomeInterest with InterestIncomeOperating.

Concept : {$fact1.concept.name}
Value : {$fact1}
Period : {$fact1.period}
Dimensions : {$fact1.dimensions.join(', ','=')}

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error
rule-focus $fact1
effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]


ASSERT US.0256.10980 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not $BDC_FLAG
	skip
else

$fact1 = {@concept = InvestmentIncomeDividend}

exists($fact1)

message
"The filer is a business development company and has reported a value of {$fact1} using the element InvestmentIncomeDividend.  This element is defined as dividend income on nonoperating securities.  For a business development company dividends earned on investments are operating income and should be tagged using the element DividendIncomeOperating. Please replace the element InvestmentIncomeDividend with DividendIncomeOperating.

Concept : {$fact1.concept.name}
Value : {$fact1}
Period : {$fact1.period}
Dimensions : {$fact1.dimensions.join(', ','=')}

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error
rule-focus $fact1
effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]


ASSERT US.0256.10981 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not $BDC_FLAG
	skip
else

$fact1 = {@concept = InvestmentIncomeInterestAndDividend}

exists($fact1)

message
"The filer is a business development company and has reported a value of {$fact1} using the element InvestmentIncomeInterestAndDividend.  This element is defined as interest and dividend income on nonoperating securities.  For a business development company interest and dividends earned on investments are operating income and should be tagged using the element InterestAndDividendIncomeOperating. Please replace the element InvestmentIncomeInterestAndDividend with InterestAndDividendIncomeOperating.

Concept : {$fact1.concept.name}
Value : {$fact1}
Period : {$fact1.period}
Dimensions : {$fact1.dimensions.join(', ','=')}

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error
rule-focus $fact1
effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]
